.TH GODEL 8 "2026-09-15" "Godel 0.9.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
godel \- static Linux init and service supervisor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B godel
.RB [ \-t
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B godel
is a static init and service supervisor written in Hare. It runs as PID 1,
parses a fixed-size configuration snapshot at boot, starts services in
dependency order, supervises them with pidfd and epoll (no allocation and no
threads after boot), and drives clean shutdown: services are stopped, then
filesystems are remounted read-only before the final
.BR sync (2)
and the
.BR reboot (2)
syscall.
.PP
When not run as PID 1,
.B godel
only validates configuration and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " PATH"
Parse-only validation of a configuration file, a configuration root, or a
.I services.d
directory. Prints
.B OK, N service(s)
on success or
.IB path : line :
.IB message
diagnostics with a nonzero exit. Nothing is started.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The boot configuration merges a single file
.I /etc/godel/services.conf
with the directory
.IR /etc/godel/services.d/ ,
scanned in name order; each directory file holds exactly one service named
after the file. A duplicate service name refuses the whole configuration.
.PP
A service section looks like:
.PP
.nf
[service "getty-tty1"]
command = /usr/bin/getty 38400 tty1
type = oneshot
restart = never
after = rootfs-rw udev-trigger
.fi
.PP
Keys:
.BR command ", " after ", " restart " ("
.BR always ", " on-failure ", " never
with
.BR restart_limit ", " restart_delay
),
.BR shutdown_timeout ", " env ", " type " ("
.B service
or
.BR oneshot
),
.BR notification-fd ", " readiness_timeout ", " run-as ", " log ".
.TP
.B after
Start ordering. A plain oneshot dependency holds its dependents until it has
run to completion (any exit status). A dependency that declares
.B notification-fd = N
(3..1024) holds its dependents until it writes a newline to fd N, bounded by
.BR readiness_timeout .
.TP
.B run-as
Drop the child to user[:group] after the cgroup attach, before
.BR execve (2).
.TP
.B log = no
Keep service output on the console instead of a per-service log file.
.PP
Hard limits are deliberate: 64 services, 8 command arguments, 4 env entries,
4
.B after
references per service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/godel/services.conf
Single-file configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/godel/services.d/
Directory configuration, merged in name order.
.TP
.I /run/godel/status
Fixed-size status snapshot, rewritten after every state change.
.TP
.I /run/godel/ctl
Control FIFO read by
.BR godelctl (8).
.TP
.I /var/log/godel/
Per-service log files (mode 0600) and the supervisor log.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration from the same sources.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Reboot.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Power off.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR godelctl (8)
